% A web shop decides on seven withdrawals from distance contracts under the
% EU Consumer Rights Directive. The 14-day withdrawal period starts on
% delivery for goods and on conclusion for a service (Article 9), and when the
% shop told the consumer about the right late, it ends 14 days after that
% (Article 10(2)). Personalised goods, unsealed hygiene goods and a fully
% performed service are excluded (Article 16). A valid withdrawal is refunded
% in full within 14 days, and the shop may withhold the refund for goods not
% yet sent back (Article 13).
% Three withdrawals are valid, one is too late and three are excluded; the
% refund of the coffee machine may be withheld.
% Shows date arithmetic with "is 14 days after", alternative rules for when a
% period starts and ends, exclusions as articles, a sum of charges and a
% negation over an open date.
% Each late notice in the scenario comes within the twelve months of Article
% 10(2); the program does not model the twelve-month cap of Article 10(1).
% Source https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2011/83/oj (Articles 9, 10, 13 and 16)

the templates are:
    *a consumer* concluded *a contract* on *a date*,
    *a contract* is a sales contract,
    *a contract* is a service contract,
    the goods of *a contract* were delivered on *a date*,
    the trader informed the consumer of the right of withdrawal from *a contract* on *a date*,
    *a contract* charged *an amount* for *a charge*,
    the goods of *a contract* were personalised for the consumer,
    the goods of *a contract* were sealed for health protection,
    the goods of *a contract* were unsealed after delivery,
    the service of *a contract* was fully performed,
    the consumer acknowledged losing the right of withdrawal from *a contract*,
    the consumer withdrew from *a contract* on *a date*,
    the consumer sent back the goods of *a contract* on *a date*,
    the withdrawal period of *a contract* starts on *a date*,
    the withdrawal period of *a contract* ends on *a date*,
    the right of withdrawal from *a contract* is excluded by *an article*,
    the withdrawal from *a contract* is valid,
    the withdrawal from *a contract* is too late,
    the trader must refund *an amount* for *a contract* by *a date*,
    the trader may withhold the refund for *a contract*.

the knowledge base consumer rights includes:

% Article 9(2)(b): for goods, the period starts when the consumer acquires
% physical possession of them.
the withdrawal period of a contract starts on a date
    if the contract is a sales contract
    and the goods of the contract were delivered on the date.

% Article 9(2)(a): for a service, it starts when the contract is concluded.
the withdrawal period of a contract starts on a date
    if the contract is a service contract
    and a consumer concluded the contract on the date.

% Article 9(1): the period runs for 14 days after its first day, when the
% consumer knew about the right from the start.
the withdrawal period of a contract ends on a date
    if the withdrawal period of the contract starts on a first date
    and the trader informed the consumer of the right of withdrawal from the contract on a second date
    and the second date is before or equal to the first date
    and the date is 14 days after the first date
    and it is not the case that
        the right of withdrawal from the contract is excluded by an article.

% Article 10(2): a late notice starts the 14 days again from its own date.
the withdrawal period of a contract ends on a date
    if the withdrawal period of the contract starts on a first date
    and the trader informed the consumer of the right of withdrawal from the contract on a second date
    and the second date is after the first date
    and the date is 14 days after the second date
    and it is not the case that
        the right of withdrawal from the contract is excluded by an article.

% Article 16(a), as amended by Directive (EU) 2019/2161: a service fully
% performed after the consumer acknowledged losing the right.
the right of withdrawal from a contract is excluded by "Article 16(a)"
    if the service of the contract was fully performed
    and the consumer acknowledged losing the right of withdrawal from the contract.

% Article 16(c): goods made to the consumer's specifications.
the right of withdrawal from a contract is excluded by "Article 16(c)"
    if the goods of the contract were personalised for the consumer.

% Article 16(e): sealed goods, unsuitable for return for health protection,
% unsealed after delivery.
the right of withdrawal from a contract is excluded by "Article 16(e)"
    if the goods of the contract were sealed for health protection
    and the goods of the contract were unsealed after delivery.

% Article 11(2): sending the withdrawal before the period ends is enough.
the withdrawal from a contract is valid
    if the consumer withdrew from the contract on a date
    and the withdrawal period of the contract ends on a second date
    and the date is before or equal to the second date.

the withdrawal from a contract is too late
    if the consumer withdrew from the contract on a date
    and the withdrawal period of the contract ends on a second date
    and the date is after the second date.

% Article 13(1): every payment, delivery included, within 14 days.
the trader must refund an amount for a contract by a date
    if the withdrawal from the contract is valid
    and the consumer withdrew from the contract on a first date
    and the date is 14 days after the first date
    and the amount is the sum of each payment such that
        the contract charged the payment for a charge.

% Article 13(3): for goods, the refund may wait until they are sent back.
the trader may withhold the refund for a contract
    if the withdrawal from the contract is valid
    and the contract is a sales contract
    and it is not the case that
        the consumer sent back the goods of the contract on a date.

scenario web shop is:
    Ana concluded the headphones order on 2026-03-01.
    the headphones order is a sales contract.
    the trader informed the consumer of the right of withdrawal from the headphones order on 2026-03-01.
    the goods of the headphones order were delivered on 2026-03-04.
    the headphones order charged 120 for goods.
    the headphones order charged 5 for delivery.
    the consumer withdrew from the headphones order on 2026-03-15.
    the consumer sent back the goods of the headphones order on 2026-03-16.

    Ben concluded the jacket order on 2026-03-01.
    the jacket order is a sales contract.
    the trader informed the consumer of the right of withdrawal from the jacket order on 2026-03-01.
    the goods of the jacket order were delivered on 2026-03-04.
    the jacket order charged 80 for goods.
    the consumer withdrew from the jacket order on 2026-03-20.

    Cleo concluded the engraved ring order on 2026-03-02.
    the engraved ring order is a sales contract.
    the trader informed the consumer of the right of withdrawal from the engraved ring order on 2026-03-02.
    the goods of the engraved ring order were delivered on 2026-03-05.
    the goods of the engraved ring order were personalised for the consumer.
    the engraved ring order charged 150 for goods.
    the consumer withdrew from the engraved ring order on 2026-03-06.

    Dirk concluded the face cream order on 2026-03-02.
    the face cream order is a sales contract.
    the trader informed the consumer of the right of withdrawal from the face cream order on 2026-03-02.
    the goods of the face cream order were delivered on 2026-03-05.
    the goods of the face cream order were sealed for health protection.
    the goods of the face cream order were unsealed after delivery.
    the face cream order charged 30 for goods.
    the consumer withdrew from the face cream order on 2026-03-09.

    Eva concluded the coffee machine order on 2026-03-01.
    the coffee machine order is a sales contract.
    the goods of the coffee machine order were delivered on 2026-03-04.
    the trader informed the consumer of the right of withdrawal from the coffee machine order on 2026-04-10.
    the coffee machine order charged 200 for goods.
    the coffee machine order charged 10 for delivery.
    the consumer withdrew from the coffee machine order on 2026-04-20.

    Finn concluded the language course order on 2026-03-02.
    the language course order is a service contract.
    the trader informed the consumer of the right of withdrawal from the language course order on 2026-03-02.
    the language course order charged 300 for tuition.
    the consumer withdrew from the language course order on 2026-03-10.

    Gert concluded the boiler repair order on 2026-03-02.
    the boiler repair order is a service contract.
    the trader informed the consumer of the right of withdrawal from the boiler repair order on 2026-03-02.
    the service of the boiler repair order was fully performed.
    the consumer acknowledged losing the right of withdrawal from the boiler repair order.
    the boiler repair order charged 90 for labour.
    the consumer withdrew from the boiler repair order on 2026-03-05.

    periods expects answers ["the withdrawal period of the headphones order ends on 2026-03-18",
        "the withdrawal period of the jacket order ends on 2026-03-18",
        "the withdrawal period of the coffee machine order ends on 2026-04-24",
        "the withdrawal period of the language course order ends on 2026-03-16"].
    excluded expects answers ["the right of withdrawal from the engraved ring order is excluded by Article 16(c)",
        "the right of withdrawal from the face cream order is excluded by Article 16(e)",
        "the right of withdrawal from the boiler repair order is excluded by Article 16(a)"].
    valid expects answers ["the withdrawal from the headphones order is valid",
        "the withdrawal from the coffee machine order is valid",
        "the withdrawal from the language course order is valid"].
    late expects answers ["the withdrawal from the jacket order is too late"].
    refunds expects answers ["the trader must refund 125 for the headphones order by 2026-03-29",
        "the trader must refund 210 for the coffee machine order by 2026-05-04",
        "the trader must refund 300 for the language course order by 2026-03-24"].
    withheld expects answers ["the trader may withhold the refund for the coffee machine order"].

query periods is:
    the withdrawal period of which contract ends on which date.

query excluded is:
    the right of withdrawal from which contract is excluded by which article.

query valid is:
    the withdrawal from which contract is valid.

query late is:
    the withdrawal from which contract is too late.

query refunds is:
    the trader must refund which amount for which contract by which date.

query withheld is:
    the trader may withhold the refund for which contract.
